1
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:13,483
Every morning, players find their check-in at the top of the app — or get it by notification, WhatsApp or email.

2
00:00:13,483 --> 00:00:17,029
One tap to start.

3
00:00:17,029 --> 00:00:25,117
Four sliders: fatigue, sleep, stress and mood. Nathan slept well and feels fresh today.

4
00:00:25,118 --> 00:00:31,022
Something hurts? Turning on Pain / Injury alerts the medical staff straight away.

5
00:00:31,022 --> 00:00:34,661
Confirm — about ten seconds in total.

6
00:00:35,063 --> 00:00:42,547
On the staff side, Team wellness gathers today’s answers and flags anyone whose 7-day trend is drifting.

7
00:00:42,547 --> 00:00:49,651
Each bar is one day. Tom’s fatigue has been rising for three days in a row.

8
00:00:49,651 --> 00:00:56,708
Readiness goes one step further: check-ins, training load and medical status become one call per player.

9
00:00:56,708 --> 00:01:05,697
Today: 2 at risk, 8 to follow up and 9 ready — Nathan, who just checked in, is one of them.

10
00:01:05,697 --> 00:01:13,164
Louis Peeters is at risk: very high fatigue and his recent load is trending up (ACWR 1.14).

11
00:01:13,164 --> 00:01:20,617
Maxime is under medical watch: pain and high fatigue, so the advice is to ease him off.

12
00:01:20,617 --> 00:01:28,102
Scroll down for players to follow up and those ready to train — every line says why.

13
00:01:28,102 --> 00:01:36,351
The same signals feed Today’s “Decide now” list, so the staff starts every morning with what needs a decision.
